@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Dependency-pair termination: proof, refutation, or honest unknown
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

component "Normalized rules\n<latex>l \to r</latex>" as RULES #DBE4FF
component "Defined RHS subterms\n<latex>l^\sharp \to u^\sharp</latex>" as PAIRS #FFF3BF
component "RewriteDependency CSR" as GRAPH #C3FAE8
component "Shared iterative\nprojection_sccs" as SCC #E5DBFF
component "Global weak obligation\n<latex>\forall(l\to r)\in R.\ I(l)\succeq I(r)</latex>" as WEAK #FFE8CC
component "Per-SCC strict obligation\n<latex>\forall(l^\sharp\to u^\sharp)\in C.\ I(l)\succ I(u)</latex>" as STRICT #FFE8CC
component "Alpha-equivalent\nroot self-cycle" as SELF #FCC2D7
component "TerminationProof" as PROOF #D3F9D8
component "NonTerminationWitness" as REFUTE #FCC2D7
component "TerminationUnknown\nunoriented SCCs + issues" as UNKNOWN #FFE3E3

RULES --> PAIRS : exact trie candidates + unification
PAIRS --> GRAPH
GRAPH --> SCC
RULES --> WEAK
SCC --> STRICT : each cyclic component
PAIRS --> SELF : concrete self dependency
WEAK --> PROOF : all weak
STRICT --> PROOF : all internal pairs strict
SELF --> REFUTE : exact repeating rewrite
SCC --> UNKNOWN : cyclic and not certified
WEAK --> UNKNOWN : weak obligation fails

note bottom of PROOF #F1F3F5
The interpretation is <latex>I(f(t_1,\ldots,t_n))=1+\sum_i I(t_i)</latex>.
An acyclic DP graph needs no cyclic certificate.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF> | normalized rewrite input |
|<#FFF3BF> | exact dependency-pair extraction |
|<#C3FAE8> | deterministic graph projection |
|<#E5DBFF> | reused SCC decomposition |
|<#FFE8CC> | reduction-pair proof obligation |
|<#D3F9D8> | proved terminating |
|<#FCC2D7> | concrete refutation path |
|<#FFE3E3> | incomplete or unavailable proof |
endlegend
@enduml
